   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Word Roller Dramatic Stop\n\nA vertical roller that fakes you out: it eases almost to a stop on the wrong word, shudders, speeds up again and finally lands on the last word with a small bounce in the accent colour and two lines drawing out to its sides.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 4 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A build-up where a ladder of words (good, better, great, amazing) ends on a legendary payoff.\n- A title card that needs suspense and a clear final word.\n\nAvoid when:\n- Neutral word swaps with no climax: use a calmer roller.\n- Long words: the window is one word wide and gets wide quickly.\n\nVariables:\n- words (string): Words, default \"Good, Better, Great, Amazing, LEGENDARY\"\n- prefix (string): Lead-in, default \"Not just good, but...\"\n- font_size (number, 16-240): Font size, default 64\n- color (color): Word color, default \"#0a0a0a\"\n- accent (color): Final color, default \"#2563eb\"\n- prefix_color (color): Lead-in color, default \"#737373\"\n- background (color): Background, default \"#fafafa\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/lifeprompt-team/remotion-scenes. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Word Roller Dramatic Stop\n\n  A vertical roller that fakes you out: it eases almost to a stop on the wrong word, shudders, speeds up again and finally lands on the last word with a small bounce in the accent colour and two lines drawing out to its sides.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/lifeprompt-team/remotion-scenes/blob/02c7a84241da7010b5f59c420b0110aafd1d6f0d/src/scenes/RollerAnimations/RollerDramaticStop.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 lifeprompt-team\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"word-roller-dramatic-stop\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"4\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"words\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Words\", \"description\": \"Words in order, separated by commas. The last one is where it settles.\", \"default\": \"Good, Better, Great, Amazing, LEGENDARY\"},\n    {\"id\": \"prefix\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Lead-in\", \"description\": \"Line above the roller.\", \"default\": \"Not just good, but...\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Size of the rolling words in pixels. A wide window shrinks to fit the frame.\", \"default\": 64, \"min\": 16, \"max\": 240, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Word color\", \"description\": \"Color of the words while they roll.\", \"default\": \"#0a0a0a\"},\n    {\"id\": \"accent\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Final color\", \"description\": \"Color of the last word and the side lines.\", \"default\": \"#2563eb\"},\n    {\"id\": \"prefix_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Lead-in color\", \"description\": \"Color of the line above.\", \"default\": \"#737373\"},\n    {\"id\": \"background\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Background\", \"description\": \"Fill behind the text. Use transparent to lay the block over your own footage.\", \"default\": \"#fafafa\"},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.05, \"unit\": \"x\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Word Roller Dramatic Stop</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@100;300;400;500;600;700;800;900&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif);\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .wds-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n\n        #root { color: var(--c, #0a0a0a); }\n        .wds-g { text-align: center; line-height: 1; position: relative; }\n        .wds-lead { font-size: 0.3125em; color: var(--pc, #737373); margin-bottom: 0.9em; white-space: pre; }\n        .wds-win { position: relative; overflow: hidden; height: 1.5625em; min-width: 6.25em; display: inline-block; vertical-align: top; }\n        .wds-mask { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; height: 0.39em; z-index: 1; }\n        .wds-mask.t { top: 0; }\n        .wds-mask.b { bottom: 0; }\n        .wds-strip { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; right: 0; }\n        .wds-item { height: 1.5625em; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; white-space: pre; }\n        .wds-line { position: absolute; top: 50%; height: 0.047em; background: var(--ac, #2563eb); display: none; transform: translateY(-50%); }\n        .wds-frame { position: relative; display: inline-block; }\n\n        .wds-sizer { display: grid; height: 0; overflow: hidden; visibility: hidden; pointer-events: none; }\n        .wds-sizer span { grid-area: 1 / 1; white-space: pre; }\n\n        .wds-sizer { padding: 0 0.5em; }\n        .wds-sizer span { font-size: 1.125em; font-weight: 700; }\n\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"word-roller-dramatic-stop\" data-duration=\"4\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"wds-clip\" class=\"wds-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"4\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"wds-g\" class=\"wds-g\">\n            <div id=\"wds-lead\" class=\"wds-lead\"></div>\n            <div class=\"wds-frame\">\n              <div class=\"wds-win\">\n                <div id=\"wds-sizer\" class=\"wds-sizer\"></div>\n                <div id=\"wds-mt\" class=\"wds-mask t\"></div>\n                <div id=\"wds-mb\" class=\"wds-mask b\"></div>\n                <div id=\"wds-strip\" class=\"wds-strip\"><div id=\"wds-i0\" class=\"wds-item\"></div><div id=\"wds-i1\" class=\"wds-item\"></div></div>\n              </div>\n              <div id=\"wds-ll\" class=\"wds-line\"></div>\n              <div id=\"wds-lr\" class=\"wds-line\"></div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function el(id) { return document.getElementById(id); }\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return value !== \"\" && value !== null && value !== undefined && Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function txt(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function list(value, fallback, max) {\n              var a = (typeof value === \"string\" ? value : \"\").split(\",\").map(function (s) { return s.trim(); }).filter(Boolean);\n              if (!a.length) a = fallback.slice();\n              return a.slice(0, max || 12);\n            }\n            function bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              return function (x) {\n                if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 32; i++) {\n                  var u = 1 - t;\n                  var cx = 3 * u * u * t * x1 + 3 * u * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                  if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                  t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                }\n                var v = 1 - t;\n                return 3 * v * v * t * y1 + 3 * v * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n              };\n            }\n            var E = {\n              out: bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), \"in\": bezier(0.7, 0, 0.84, 0), inOut: bezier(0.87, 0, 0.13, 1),\n              overshoot: bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1), smooth: bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1),\n              quadIn: function (x) { return x * x; },\n              quadOut: function (x) { return 1 - (1 - x) * (1 - x); },\n              cubicOut: function (x) { return 1 - Math.pow(1 - x, 3); },\n              cubicInOut: function (x) { return x < 0.5 ? 4 * x * x * x : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * x + 2, 3) / 2; }\n            };\n            function clamp01(p) { return Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p)); }\n            // the source framework interpolate with clamped ends, one input range and one output range.\n            function ip(x, a, b, from, to, ease) {\n              var p = b === a ? (x >= b ? 1 : 0) : clamp01((x - a) / (b - a));\n              return from + (to - from) * (ease ? ease(p) : p);\n            }\n            // Damped spring from 0 towards 1 (mass, stiffness, damping), frame at 30 fps, in closed form.\n            function spring(frame, cfg) {\n              if (frame <= 0) return 0;\n              var t = frame / 30, m = cfg.mass || 1, k = cfg.stiffness === undefined ? 100 : cfg.stiffness, c = cfg.damping === undefined ? 10 : cfg.damping;\n              var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / m), z = c / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * m));\n              if (Math.abs(z - 1) < 1e-6) return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n              if (z < 1) {\n                var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n                return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + (z * w0 / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n              }\n              var q = w0 * Math.sqrt(z * z - 1), r1 = -z * w0 + q, r2 = -z * w0 - q;\n              return 1 - (r2 * Math.exp(r1 * t) - r1 * Math.exp(r2 * t)) / (r2 - r1);\n            }\n            // Seeded generator (mulberry32).\n            function rng(seed) {\n              var a = seed >>> 0;\n              return function () {\n                a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n                var t = a;\n                t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n                t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n                return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n              };\n            }\n            function onFonts(fn) {\n              if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) document.fonts.ready.then(fn, function () {});\n            }\n            // Sets the group's font size, then shrinks it so the group (or its probe) fits the frame.\n            function fitG(g, size, probe, wf, hf, wmul) {\n              g.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var p = probe || g;\n              var w = Math.max(1, p.offsetWidth * (wmul || 1)), h = Math.max(1, p.offsetHeight);\n              var k = Math.min(1, root.clientWidth * (wf || 0.9) / w, root.clientHeight * (hf || 0.9) / h);\n              if (k < 1) { size = Math.max(6, size * k); g.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; }\n              return size;\n            }\n            function fillSizer(sizer, words) {\n              sizer.textContent = \"\";\n              words.forEach(function (w) {\n                var s = document.createElement(\"span\");\n                s.textContent = w;\n                sizer.appendChild(s);\n              });\n            }\n            function setText(node, value) {\n              if (node.__t !== value) { node.__t = value; node.textContent = value; }\n            }\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"4\");\n            var clock = { frame: 0 };\n            function start(draw) {\n              var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: Math.round(TOTAL * 30), duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(Math.round(clock.frame * speed * 1000) / 1000); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"word-roller-dramatic-stop\"] = tl;\n            }\n\n            root.style.background = str(vars.background, \"#fafafa\");\n            \n            var words = list(vars.words, [\"Good\", \"Better\", \"Great\", \"Amazing\", \"LEGENDARY\"], 10);\n            var fi = words.length - 1;\n            var g = el(\"wds-g\"), lead = el(\"wds-lead\"), strip = el(\"wds-strip\"), i0 = el(\"wds-i0\"), i1 = el(\"wds-i1\"), ll = el(\"wds-ll\"), lr = el(\"wds-lr\");\n            var color = str(vars.color, \"#0a0a0a\"), accent = str(vars.accent, \"#2563eb\");\n            root.style.setProperty(\"--c\", color);\n            root.style.setProperty(\"--ac\", accent);\n            if (typeof vars.prefix_color === \"string\" && vars.prefix_color) root.style.setProperty(\"--pc\", vars.prefix_color);\n            var bg = str(vars.background, \"#fafafa\");\n            el(\"wds-mt\").style.background = \"linear-gradient(\" + bg + \", transparent)\";\n            el(\"wds-mb\").style.background = \"linear-gradient(transparent, \" + bg + \")\";\n            lead.textContent = txt(vars.prefix, \"Not just good, but...\");\n            lead.style.display = lead.textContent ? \"\" : \"none\";\n            fillSizer(el(\"wds-sizer\"), words);\n            var base = num(vars.font_size, 64, 16, 240);\n            function fit() {\n              g.style.fontSize = base + \"px\";\n              var need = g.offsetWidth + 3.4 * base;\n              var k = Math.min(1, root.clientWidth * 0.9 / Math.max(1, need), root.clientHeight * 0.8 / Math.max(1, g.offsetHeight));\n              g.style.fontSize = Math.max(6, base * k) + \"px\";\n            }\n            fit();\n            onFonts(fit);\n\n            function sty(node, idx, fin, emph) {\n              var last = idx === fi;\n              setText(node, words[idx]);\n              node.style.fontSize = (last && fin ? 1.125 : 1) + \"em\";\n              node.style.height = (1.5625 / (last && fin ? 1.125 : 1)) + \"em\";\n              node.style.fontWeight = last ? 700 : 500;\n              node.style.color = last ? accent : color;\n              node.style.transform = last && fin ? \"scale(\" + (1 + emph * 0.1) + \")\" : \"none\";\n            }\n            // remocn-scenes: four phases (slow start, a near stop around 20-25 %, a re-acceleration, then a\n            // long ease-out), a damped bounce over the last 10 frames, and a spring-in emphasis at the end.\n            function ease(x) {\n              if (x < 0.25) return 0.2 * E.quadOut(x / 0.25);\n              if (x < 0.4375) return 0.2 + 0.05 * (1 - Math.pow(1 - (x - 0.25) / 0.1875, 3));\n              if (x < 0.5625) return 0.25 + 0.1 * E.quadIn((x - 0.4375) / 0.125);\n              return 0.35 + 0.65 * (1 - Math.pow(1 - (x - 0.5625) / 0.4375, 4));\n            }\n            function draw(f) {\n              var WH = 100, D = 80, total = fi * WH;\n              var scrollY = ease(clamp01(f / D)) * total;\n              if (f >= D - 10) {\n                var bp = spring(f - (D - 10), { damping: 12, stiffness: 200 });\n                scrollY = total + 15 * (1 - bp) * Math.sin((f - (D - 10)) * 0.5);\n              }\n              if (f >= D) scrollY = total;\n              var di = Math.min(Math.floor(scrollY / WH), fi);\n              var off = scrollY % WH;\n              var fin = f >= D;\n              var emph = fin ? spring(f - D, { damping: 8, stiffness: 150 }) : 0;\n              sty(i0, di, fin, emph);\n              i1.style.display = di < fi ? \"\" : \"none\";\n              if (di < fi) sty(i1, Math.min(di + 1, fi), false, 0);\n              strip.style.transform = \"translateY(\" + (-off / 64) + \"em)\";\n              var shake = f >= 20 && f < 35 ? Math.sin(f * 2) * 2 * (1 - (f - 20) / 15) : 0;\n              g.style.transform = \"translateX(\" + (shake / 64) + \"em)\";\n              lead.style.opacity = ip(f, 0, 15, 0, 1);\n              var show = fin && di === fi;\n              ll.style.display = lr.style.display = show ? \"block\" : \"none\";\n              ll.style.left = \"-1.5625em\";\n              lr.style.right = \"-1.5625em\";\n              ll.style.width = lr.style.width = (60 * emph / 64) + \"em\";\n            }\n            start(draw);\n\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
